{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(s: str, ch: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrence of a given character from the string.\"\"\"\n    fi = s.find(ch)\n    if fi == -1:\n        return s\n\n    li = s.rfind(ch)\n\n    if fi == li:\n        # Character appears only once, remove that single occurrence\n        return s[:fi] + s[fi+1:]\n    else:\n        # Remove both first and last occurrences\n        return s[:fi] + s[fi+1:li] + s[li+1:]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "def find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum number of positive rotations required to get the same string.\n    This uses the KMP prefix function to determine the string's minimal period.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        # According to design, empty string is invalid, but for a single function without\n        # error handling specified as part of the function itself, returning 0 or 1\n        # might be implicit, or relying on external validation.\n        # Given \"minimum number of rotations (greater than 0)\", an empty string technically has no rotations.\n        # However, the problem statement implies non-empty strings based on assertions.\n        # The design context says \"minimal positive rotation count for a non-empty string\"\n        # and \"Empty string is invalid input.\" But the prompt specifically forbids\n        # raising exceptions or `isinstance` checks. So, assuming valid non-empty string as per constraints.\n        return 0 # Or handle as per broader system spec if integrated\n\n    pi = [0] * n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        j = pi[i - 1]\n        while j > 0 and s[i] != s[j]:\n            j = pi[j - 1]\n        if s[i] == s[j]:\n            j += 1\n        pi[i] = j\n\n    period = n - pi[n - 1]\n    \n    # If the string length is a multiple of its period, the period is the answer.\n    # Otherwise, the string does not consist of repetitions of a smaller substring,\n    # so the only way to get the same string is to rotate it by its full length.\n    if n % period == 0:\n        return period\n    else:\n        return n"}
