{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts substrings where the sum of digits equals their length.\n    Uses the prefix sum technique after transforming digits to (digit - 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    # Stores the frequency of each prefix sum encountered so far.\n    # Initialize with {0: 1} to account for substrings starting from index 0\n    # (i.e., when prefix_sum[j+1] == prefix_sum[0]).\n    freq = {0: 1}\n    \n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    total_count = 0\n\n    for char_digit in s:\n        # Convert character digit to integer and adjust by -1.\n        # ord(char_digit) - ord('0') is an efficient way to convert char to int.\n        adjusted_value = (ord(char_digit) - ord('0')) - 1\n        \n        current_prefix_sum += adjusted_value\n        \n        # If current_prefix_sum has been seen before, it means there are\n        # substrings ending here whose (digit sum - length) is 0.\n        # Add the count of previous occurrences of this prefix sum.\n        total_count += freq.get(current_prefix_sum, 0)\n        \n        # Increment the frequency for the current prefix sum.\n        freq[current_prefix_sum] = freq.get(current_prefix_sum, 0) + 1\n        \n    return total_count"}
