{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(values: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in a list of integers.\"\"\"\n    num_zeros = 0\n    num_non_zeros = 0\n    for value in values:\n        if value == 0:\n            num_zeros += 1\n        else:\n            num_non_zeros += 1\n\n    if num_non_zeros == 0:\n        # If there are no non-zero elements, division by zero occurs.\n        # Python's float division handles 0/0 as NaN and X/0 as inf,\n        # adhering to the constraint not to raise exceptions for edge cases.\n        return float(num_zeros) / float(num_non_zeros)\n    \n    return float(num_zeros) / float(num_non_zeros)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/140", "solution": "from typing import Iterable, Set, Union\ndef extract_singly(items: Iterable[Iterable[object]], allow_str_numbers: bool = False) -> Set[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"Flattens a list of lists into a single set of numbers.\n    Assumes elements are numeric or directly convertible, per constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_set: Set[Union[int, float]] = set()\n    for inner_list in items:\n        for element in inner_list:\n            result_set.add(element)\n    return result_set"}
