{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element x is the majority element in the first n elements of a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Helper function for binary search to find the lower bound of x in the first 'count' elements.\n    # It returns the index of the first element >= x, or 'count' if no such element exists.\n    def _lower_bound(array: list[int], count: int, target: int) -> int:\n        low, high = 0, count\n        while low < high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if array[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid\n        return low\n\n    # Find the index of the first occurrence of x in the first 'n' elements.\n    first_occurrence_index = _lower_bound(arr, n, x)\n\n    # If x is not found (first_occurrence_index is 'n' or arr[first_occurrence_index] is not x),\n    # then it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_occurrence_index == n or arr[first_occurrence_index] != x:\n        return False\n\n    # Calculate the index that would be n/2 positions after the first occurrence.\n    # If arr[first_occurrence_index + n//2] is still x, it means x occurs\n    # more than n/2 times (i.e., at least n//2 + 1 times).\n    majority_check_index = first_occurrence_index + n // 2\n\n    # Check if this calculated index is within the bounds [0, n)\n    # and if the element at this index is indeed x.\n    return majority_check_index < n and arr[majority_check_index] == x"}
