{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(n):\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of a number.\n    Negative numbers are treated by their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    num = abs(n)\n\n    # Use the built-in bit_count method if available (Python 3.8+)\n    if hasattr(num, 'bit_count'):\n        return num.bit_count()\n    else:\n        # Fallback to Kernighan's algorithm for older Python versions\n        count = 0\n        while num > 0:\n            num &= (num - 1)\n            count += 1\n        return count"}
