{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(pairs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maps each unique, normalized tuple (min, max) to its occurrence count.\n    Treats (a, b) and (b, a) as the same, normalizing them to (min, max).\n    \"\"\"\n    from collections import defaultdict\n\n    counts = defaultdict(int)\n\n    for item in pairs:\n        # Normalize the pair by ordering its elements\n        a, b = item\n        normalized_key = (a, b) if a <= b else (b, a)\n        counts[normalized_key] += 1\n\n    return dict(counts)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n, width=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (1-based positions 2, 4, 6...) of a non-negative integer.\n    The mask's width is determined by the input number's bit length or an optional width.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _inferred_width(num):\n        # Determines the minimum width for the mask based on the number's bit length.\n        # Ensures a minimum width of 2 to cover the first even bit position.\n        return max(2, num.bit_length())\n\n    def _compute_mask_for_width(w):\n        # Generates a mask with bits set at 0-based indices 1, 3, 5, ... up to w-1.\n        mask = 0\n        for i in range(w):\n            if (i % 2) == 1:  # Check for 0-based odd indices (1-based even positions)\n                mask |= (1 << i)\n        return mask\n\n    # Determine the effective width for mask generation.\n    # If width is not provided, infer it from 'n'.\n    use_width = width if width is not None else _inferred_width(n)\n\n    # Compute the mask with relevant bits set.\n    mask_to_apply = _compute_mask_for_width(use_width)\n\n    # Apply the mask using a bitwise OR operation.\n    return n | mask_to_apply"}
