{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of possible sequences of length n, such that each element is a positive integer\n    and is greater than or equal to twice the previous element but less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class InMemoryCache:\n        \"\"\"A simple in-memory cache for memoization.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self):\n            self._store = {}\n\n        def get(self, key: tuple[int, int]) -> int | None:\n            return self._store.get(key)\n\n        def set(self, key: tuple[int, int], value: int) -> None:\n            self._store[key] = value\n\n        def clear(self) -> None:\n            self._store.clear()\n\n    class SequenceService:\n        \"\"\"Core algorithm for counting sequences using dynamic programming with memoization.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, cache: InMemoryCache):\n            self._cache = cache\n            self._m = 0 # Max value for sequence elements, set by count_sequences\n\n        def count_sequences(self, m_val: int, n_val: int) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Entry point to compute the total number of sequences.\"\"\"\n            self._m = m_val\n            self._cache.clear() # Ensure cache is fresh for each new top-level request\n            # Start recursion with 'n_val' remaining elements and '1' as the minimum possible value for the first element.\n            return self._count_recursive(n_val, 1)\n\n        def _count_recursive(self, remaining: int, min_value: int) -> int:\n            \"\"\"\n            Recursive helper to count sequences.\n            'remaining' is the number of elements yet to be placed in the sequence.\n            'min_value' is the minimum allowed value for the current element.\n            \"\"\"\n            # Base case 1: If no more elements are remaining, a valid sequence has been formed.\n            if remaining == 0:\n                return 1\n            # Base case 2: If the minimum required value exceeds the maximum allowed (m),\n            # no valid element can be placed, so this path yields no sequences.\n            if min_value > self._m:\n                return 0\n\n            key = (remaining, min_value)\n            cached_result = self._cache.get(key)\n            if cached_result is not None:\n                return cached_result\n\n            total_sequences = 0\n            # Iterate through all possible values (x) for the current element.\n            # x must be at least min_value and at most self._m.\n            for x in range(min_value, self._m + 1):\n                # For the next element in the sequence, its minimum value must be 2*x.\n                total_sequences += self._count_recursive(remaining - 1, 2 * x)\n\n            self._cache.set(key, total_sequences)\n            return total_sequences\n\n    # Instantiate the cache and the service, then call the main counting method.\n    cache_instance = InMemoryCache()\n    service_instance = SequenceService(cache_instance)\n    return service_instance.count_sequences(m, n)"}
