{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next perfect square strictly greater than the given integer n.\n    It is assumed that n is an integer based on the design context.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        # For any negative integer, the smallest perfect square (0) is strictly greater.\n        return 0\n    else:\n        # Calculate the integer square root of n (floor(sqrt(n))).\n        r = math.isqrt(n)\n        # The next perfect square is (r + 1)^2. This correctly handles cases\n        # where n is a perfect square (e.g., n=36, r=6, next is 49)\n        # and where n is not (e.g., n=35, r=5, next is 36).\n        return (r + 1) * (r + 1)"}
