{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "_lucas_cache = {0: 2, 1: 1}\ndef find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n'th Lucas number using an iterative approach with memoization.\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer as per design context.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _lucas_cache:\n        return _lucas_cache[n]\n\n    # Find the largest index already in cache to continue computation from.\n    max_cached_n = max(_lucas_cache.keys())\n\n    # Initialize prev2 and prev1 with the last two computed Lucas numbers,\n    # and determine the starting index for the loop.\n    # If only L0 is in cache (shouldn't happen with {0:2, 1:1} initialisation, but robust check),\n    # start from L0 and L1.\n    if max_cached_n < 1:\n        prev2, prev1 = _lucas_cache[0], _lucas_cache[1]\n        start_idx = 2\n    else:\n        prev2, prev1 = _lucas_cache[max_cached_n - 1], _lucas_cache[max_cached_n]\n        start_idx = max_cached_n + 1\n\n    # Iteratively compute Lucas numbers from start_idx up to n, caching each result.\n    for i in range(start_idx, n + 1):\n        current_lucas = prev1 + prev2\n        _lucas_cache[i] = current_lucas\n        prev2 = prev1\n        prev1 = current_lucas\n    \n    return _lucas_cache[n]"}
