{"task_id": "Mbpp/418", "solution": "def Find_Max(elements):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element in a list that has the maximum length.\n    Returns the first element encountered with the maximum length if there are ties.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_element = elements[0]\n    max_length = len(elements[0])\n\n    for i in range(1, len(elements)):\n        current_element = elements[i]\n        current_length = len(current_element)\n        if current_length > max_length:\n            max_length = current_length\n            max_element = current_element\n            \n    return max_element"}
