{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def tuple_intersection(list_a: List[Tuple[int, int]], list_b: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> Set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of two lists of 2-element tuples, treating (a,b) and (b,a) as equal.\n    Returns a set of canonical (sorted) tuples found in both input lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    def _to_canonical_set(tuples: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> Set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n        \"\"\"Normalizes each tuple to (min, max) order and collects them in a set.\"\"\"\n        canonical_set = set()\n        for pair in tuples:\n            normalized_pair = tuple(sorted(pair))\n            canonical_set.add(normalized_pair)\n        return canonical_set\n\n    canonical_set_a = _to_canonical_set(list_a)\n    canonical_set_b = _to_canonical_set(list_b)\n\n    return canonical_set_a.intersection(canonical_set_b)"}
