{"task_id": "Mbpp/475", "solution": "from typing import Mapping, List, Tuple\ndef sort_counter(mapping: Mapping[str, int], *, reverse: bool = True, tie_break: str = \"key\") -> List[Tuple[str, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a dictionary by its values, with an optional tie-breaker by key.\n    Returns a list of (key, value) tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    items = list(mapping.items())\n\n    if tie_break == \"key\":\n        if reverse:\n            # Sort descending by value, then ascending by key for ties\n            items.sort(key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0]))\n        else:\n            # Sort ascending by value, then ascending by key for ties\n            items.sort(key=lambda kv: (kv[1], kv[0]))\n    else:\n        # Sort by value, using the 'reverse' flag directly.\n        # Python's sort is stable, so original order is preserved for ties if no secondary key is specified.\n        items.sort(key=lambda kv: kv[1], reverse=reverse)\n\n    return items"}
