{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "from collections import Counter\ndef count_Pairs(numbers, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of possible unordered pairs where both elements are unequal.\n    This function computes the total possible pairs and subtracts pairs of equal elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def choose2(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper to calculate k * (k - 1) // 2, which is the number of ways to choose 2 items from k.\"\"\"\n        if k < 2:\n            return 0\n        return (k * (k - 1)) // 2\n\n    total_possible_pairs = choose2(n)\n    \n    # Count frequencies of each number\n    frequencies = Counter(numbers)\n    \n    # Calculate pairs of equal elements\n    duplicate_pairs = sum(choose2(count) for count in frequencies.values())\n    \n    return total_possible_pairs - duplicate_pairs"}
