{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by k positions.\n    Handles empty lists, and k values greater than or less than list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Normalize k to be within [0, n-1].\n    # The modulo operator correctly handles both positive k > n and negative k.\n    normalized_k = k % n\n\n    # Perform the rotation using list slicing.\n    return lst[-normalized_k:] + lst[:-normalized_k]"}
